reports/
# ...EXCEPT the two things a BUILD GATE reads. `ci/no-bare-absence.sh` resolves every
# `ledger:<row_id>` citation against the validation ledger, and the host-function registry
# refuses to load a function whose mutation score is not a produced file. A gate whose data is
# gitignored passes vacuously in a fresh clone — which is this project's own failure mode
# applied to its own CI. Found at P4 by asking what a clone would not have.
!reports/validation-ledger.jsonl
!reports/host_fns/
!reports/host_fns/*.json
blobs/
*.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mutmut-cache
# fixtures/ is NEVER ignored — the nine real artifacts are the evidence base
!fixtures/
.DS_Store
.hypothesis/
